{"name":"Statuesque","hex":"#e0dfd9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"statuesque","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Resembling or characteristic of a statue. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Immobile; motionless."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/statuesque"}],"entries":[{"title":"Statuesque","blocks":[{"text":"\"Statuesque\" is a song by Britpop band Sleeper, written by the band's vocalist and guitarist, Louise Wener. \"Statuesque\" was the fourth and final single to be released from Sleeper's second album, The It Girl, and became the group's last top-20 hit on the UK Singles Chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b6/Statuesque7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statuesque"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"statuesque":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f3/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-NaomiAmethyst-statuesque.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f3/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-NaomiAmethyst-statuesque.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-NaomiAmethyst-statuesque.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f3/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-NaomiAmethyst-statuesque.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-NaomiAmethyst-statuesque.wav.ogg"}]}}}